so I've been using my new iPhone 14 pro  Max for the last couple of months and to  be completely honest I thought the brand  new changes and features that Apple  added this time around would be a much  bigger deal in terms of how I use my  phone every day and the overall quality  of life improvements now don't get me  wrong there are some changes that I'm  actually very happy about and I don't  regret upgrading at all even though  there are a couple of drawbacks compared  to the previous model but let's start  with the good stuff first now by far the  biggest change that I've been waiting  for for years now was the always on  display and it's finally here the only  thing that surprised me was that despite  Apple's Best in Class technique for how  it works specifically being able to go  down to one Hertz display refresh rate  when using the always-on display it  still had a noticeable hit to my battery  life because of that I decided to create  a custom Focus this mode that doesn't do  anything but change the wallpaper to an  all black wallpaper with red text and an  effort to save battery life since red  LED light uses the least amount of power  and voltage leading to the most battery  life savings now thankfully over the  past two months Apple has released some  new updates that have definitely helped  with battery life and it's safe to say  that it's now almost as good as it was  with the 13 Pro Max but I find myself  still using this black wallpaper setup  since I'm so used to it and I still  really like it especially for the  contrast on the home page but as far as  quality of life improvements it's really  helped me in two ways the first one is  that I no longer accidentally forget  about notifications that previously  popped up for a few moments before the  screen turned off because now they stay  there on the display so I'm constantly  reminded of them and that helps me with  my issue of forgetting to reply to  Notifications now the second quality of  life Improvement is the fact that I can  Now swipe to wake and unlock the phone  with just a single swipe whereas  previously you'd have to tap first to  wake it up and then swipe to unlock now  I know first world problems but it has  made it so much more convenient to  unlock my phone when I'm at my desk now  moving on from that we've got to talk  about the dynamic Island which at first  seemed so cool and convenient when Apple  showed it off making it seem like it  would always be useful but it just  doesn't seem like it's been that useful  for me but now that I actually think a  little bit more deeply about it it's  been extremely useful in a passive sense  for example the worst thing in the world  used to be the low battery pop-up that  would take up the entire display and  force you to press ok but now it simply  just pops up in the island without  bugging you same thing for the little  face ID notification which pops up  subtly at the top as well as the ringer  vol volume indicator it just gives those  previously annoying things a better more  subtle location and I really like that  on top of that the island has been  extremely useful because it gives you a  convenient way to quickly open up the  app that's using it like for example  going directly into the music app  instead of swiping through the app  switcher to find it and also when you're  on a phone call you can quickly tap on  the island and go back to it if you need  to quickly switch the Bluetooth Source  or anything else and my personal  favorite having the timer always show  the countdown of seconds at the top has  been invaluable but other than that  there hasn't been much use to it and I'm  actually more happy about the removal of  the ugly Notch especially since the new  speaker Grille is Razor thin and hardly  noticeable which I love and surprisingly  the speakers have gotten even louder and  better across the board in terms of  sound quality and I like like to use my  iPhone speakers a lot when watching  YouTube videos so I enjoy that change  now my favorite iPhone feature is still  Mac safe because I love using it with my  macsafe wallet and especially my  wireless charger in the car but our  sponsor base us has this awesome new  Mega attached 20 watt magnetic wireless  charging power bank with 10 000  milliamps of power that holds on very  well and automatically charges your  iPhone at up to 7.5 Watts or 15 watts  for Androids it also has a nice foldable  kickstand built in for watching videos a  nice LED status light indicator and even  20 watt PD full fast charging using a  cable to plug it in directly from the  power bank to your iPhone they've also  got their six in one power combo 40 watt  power strip which can charge up to six  devices is including 20 watt fast  charging two of them at once since it  has two USBC ports a USB a port and  three power outlets right on the Strip  itself for plugging in anything you'd  like so it works like an extension cable  but with surge protection built in and  of course the extra three USB ports  which is awesome so be sure to check out  both the power strip and Max life  battery Bank using the links below now  one of the major downsides of the new  iPhone 14 models that I didn't think  would be a problem is the fact that  Apple got rid of the SIM card slot  forcing people to use e-sim now I myself  had some issues with slow cell service  for the first week of owning this phone  but over the past couple months two of  my family members upgraded to new iPhone  14 Pro Models and both of them had major  issues with connecting their service  because of a lack of the SIM card slot  and because of that they either had to  call in in or walk into their service  provider's office to get it working  which is of course extremely annoying  now as far as the actual performance of  the iPhone 14 pro I literally haven't  noticed any difference in actual speed  or snappiness of this iPhone compared to  the previous one but I'm pleasantly  surprised and satisfied with the big  Improvement in cooling since I've rarely  had the display on the 14 pro Max dim  compared to last year when it would  happen on occasion but now it rarely  ever happens mostly when I'm in direct  sunlight on a very hot summer day now  the new camera changes are where I was a  little bit disappointed but at the same  time extremely satisfied so let me  explain what I mean in some aspects of  the camera there is a negligible  difference compared to the previous  model like using the main camera in  broad daylight but with all of the other  cameras I'm seeing some improvements  especially with the ultra wide camera at  night which used to struggle a lot the  selfie camera also now has a really nice  level of detail and sharpness compared  to before so it's now nice and  competitive against the competition like  the s22 ultra which used to always  destroy the iPhone for selfies but out  of everything I take portrait mode  photos the most and I'm extremely happy  about how well portraits turn out with  improvements to the blur edging and  especially the color reproduction and  glow during the sunset golden hour and I  really appreciate that Apple added the  2x crop mode button that also works with  portraits if you want a specific Zoom  length so it's very convenient and by  the way the 2x crop mode actually works  and greatly improves the quality  compared to previously but a major game  changing feature this year is the new 48  megapixel Pro raw photo feature which  gives you extremely detailed photos  using the main camera and this has  already come in handy to take group  photos of people with insane amounts of  detail now initially I was annoyed by  this feature because Apple forces you to  shoot in the Pro raw format which uses a  massive amount of storage but I  discovered a shortcut that can bulk  convert those files into heic files that  barely take up any storage but retain  most of the detail so I'm gonna add a  link in the description to how to create  that shortcut and finally I'm really  disappointed that Apple didn't give us  8K video recording even though the new  48 megapixel sensor was basically built  for it so I'm sure it's coming next year  but at least the 4K recording still  beats out the competition so I guess it  doesn't matter that much and I'm so glad  that cinematic mode finally supports 4K  resolution so it's 5 finally viable and  looks really good compared to portrait  video on any other phone now one  drawback that Max mentioned in a  previous video is the display glass  quality being easier to scratch and yes  I have noticed that it scratches easier  especially when I dropped it onto gravel  you could probably notice in the b-roll  of this video that it is scratched up  but despite all of that my experience  has been good and I feel like I've  enjoyed more of the passive features of  the new 14 pro Max compared to the  features that Apple actually focused on  in their presentation and despite the  limited number of drawbacks I'm still  very happy with this upgrade and looking  forward to what Apple's gonna come out  with next year so hopefully you enjoy  this two month review and if you did go  ahead and click the circle above to  subscribe for more videos like this one  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

